<title>GERMANY: Striking German NATO workers protest in Bonn.</title>
<headline>Striking German NATO workers protest in Bonn.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven thousand civilian workers from United States and British NATO bases in Germany demonstrated in Bonn on Wednesday against cost-cutting measures planned by their employers, unions said.</p>
<p>The one-hour protest through streets in central Bonn followed the restart of strike action by some 4,000 workers on Tuesday after negotiations between unions and employer representatives collapsed last week.</p>
<p>Around 35,000 civilians, mostly German, are employed by NATO allies across the country. Many civilians working at the bases have already lost their jobs as NATO forces in Germany have been cut back since the end of the Cold War.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
